{
  "sn42.9:0.1": "Linked Discourses 42.9 ",
  "sn42.9:0.2": "1. Chiefs ",
  "sn42.9:0.3": "Families ",
  "sn42.9:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the land of the Kosalans together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants when he arrived at Nāḷandā. ",
  "sn42.9:1.2": "There he stayed near Nāḷandā in Pāvārika’s Mango Grove. ",
  "sn42.9:2.1": "Now at that time Nāḷandā was undergoing famine and scarcity, with crops blighted and turned to straw. ",
  "sn42.9:2.2": "At that time the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan was residing at Nāḷandā together with a large assembly of Jain ascetics. ",
  "sn42.9:2.3": "Then Asibandhaka’s son the chief, who was a disciple of the Jains, went up to the Jain Ñātika, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Jain Ñātika said to him: ",
  "sn42.9:2.4": "“Come, chief, refute the ascetic Gotama’s doctrine. ",
  "sn42.9:2.5": "Then you will get a good reputation: ",
  "sn42.9:2.6": "‘Asibandhaka’s son the chief refuted the doctrine of the ascetic Gotama, so mighty and powerful!’” ",
  "sn42.9:3.1": "“But sir, how am I to do this?” ",
  "sn42.9:3.2": "“Here, brahmin, go to the ascetic Gotama and say to him: ",
  "sn42.9:3.3": "‘Sir, don’t you in many ways praise kindness, protection, and sympathy for families?’ ",
  "sn42.9:3.4": "When he’s asked this, if he answers: ",
  "sn42.9:3.5": "‘Indeed I do, chief,’ say this to him: ",
  "sn42.9:3.6": "‘So what then are you doing, wandering together with this large Saṅgha of mendi